# Line endings that must not depend on the machine (wave 43).
#
# The commit hook is a shell script. Checked out with Windows line endings
# (git's core.autocrlf=true does that), "sh" reads "set -e\r" and the hook
# fails on every commit, or is skipped. These files always keep LF.
hooks/pre-commit  text eol=lf
*.sh              text eol=lf
